+# System-feel extracted-legacy reference (Task 4)
+
+## Run and evidence
+
+From repository root:
+
+```sh
+lmf/migrations/hcwp/system-feel/characterise/verify --evidence-prefix my-fresh-run
+```
+
+Requires Python 3 and .NET SDK 10 (this execution: 10.0.401). No external NuGet packages, application project references, Oracle, EF provider, browser or Windows UI are used. `verify` runs the complete input membership/hash/immutable approval and citation gate, verifies reproducible extraction, checks all five Task-3 contract artifact digests, builds the reference, then executes every SF-001–SF-053 definition. No absent prerequisite becomes a skip. Unknown operations, missing groups/IDs, empty expectations or runtime errors fail. The process returns nonzero unless all 53 execute with positive passes, zero failures and zero skips.
+
+Results: `<prefix>-reference-results.json` (counts, groups, exact commands/times, Python and logged .NET versions, source/contract hashes); `<prefix>-reference-observations.json` (every actual and expected observation, classification and failures); `<prefix>-reference-verification.log` (integrity/extraction/build/runtime output). Integrity/citation files use `<prefix>-reference-*` destinations. All evidence is exclusive-create and destinations are preflighted before work. Use a new prefix on reruns; never delete or replace retained attempts. Compiler `bin/` and `obj/`, interpreter caches and `.py[cod]` files are excluded from source binding. No baseline evidence writer is invoked. The original 40 KD03 definitions remain unchanged; this task executes the 53 new extension scenarios, not the final-application 40-scenario regression suite.
+
+## Extraction and adaptations
+
+`extract.py` does not read fixtures or expectations. `original/C*.txt` are exact LF-normalised physical source spans from the bound original bundles. `extraction-manifest.json` records original paths, physical coordinates, source digests, symbols/fragments and extracted digests. Default extraction mode regenerates in memory and compares every artifact byte-for-byte; `--capture` refuses any existing output. The full source citation and input integrity gates execute before this check. `Legacy.cs` is reproducibly generated C#, not handwritten translations or code copied from the migrated target. The complete GetKdpResults method is retained and executed. Original snippets remain alongside the generated code for inspection.
+
+| Original rule / evidence | Actual executable extraction or explicit adaptation |
+| --- | --- |
+| StandardNameResolver C005 | Original ResolveCore body compiled unchanged; method renamed `Legacy.Name`, INameModel replaced by compatibility ChildGeneral. Exact null/empty concatenation and trailing separator retained. |
+| AddressResolver C008 | Original ResolveCore body compiled unchanged as `Legacy.Address`; AddressModel replaced by compatibility ChildGeneral with the same six fields. No trimming/normalising addition. |
+| AgeResolver C012 | Complete GetAge method compiled, visibility made public; only `DateTime.Now` replaced by `ReferenceClock.Now`. .NET integer division, Gregorian wall-clock dates, death threshold precedence, month arithmetic and text retained. Does not implement missing Oracle Lookups.Age. |
+| GetOrganisationValue C017 | Complete method compiled; visibility public. Cast of named centre constant to byte removed: the unavailable numeric constant is represented by the named string HEALTH_AUTHORITY. First matching centre, linked Organisation, single authority-Y lookup and exact join/dash branches remain. Duplicate matching authority rows still throw. |
+| ChildCentreResolver C015 | Both methods retained. School return type becomes object; missing CodeDescriptionFormat call replaced by `Resource.Format(identity,args)`, preserving code/null-linked-name and absent-centre dash. This is NOT recovered legacy punctuation/prose. |
+| ClientSummaryModel.ShowAlert C018 | Exact property expression compiled in AlertModel. Named status constants are distinct symbolic strings, never invented numeric codes; source Any() still applies to the supplied nonnull alert list. |
+| KdpExaminationService.GetKdpExamination C021 | Exact `.Where(patient AND KDP).OrderByDescending(given date).ToList()` expression compiled against synthetic entity/navigation graph in ResultService. Service hosting, includes, consent/appointments and unrelated parent metadata are outside this query observation. Graph rows are committed-query inputs, not form submissions. |
+| KdpExaminationDelegate.GetKdpResults C022 | Complete method compiled, unchanged. ResultTO, service and delegate construction scaffolding deliver saved rows without adding an ordering key. SF-038 separately parses every ordering call in the bound complete original method, emitting keys and absence of tie keys. Runtime groups compare complete tie membership, not observed tie order. |
+| PhysicalAssessment6To8Weeks C027 | Complete source lookup method compiled unchanged. Physical fields from C029/C030 are passed through nullable saved values using this dictionary. No female-Testes rejection, null-to-3 conversion or social-field inclusion is added. |
+| StaticSpan C010 | Only nonempty/null/empty text branch extracted; TagBuilder.SetInnerText becomes assignment and returns text. No HTML encoding/attributes, DateTime-MinValue, MVC control, accessibility or rendering equivalence claimed. Format-null string cases only are covered here. |
+| GetClientSummary C001; WebProfile C003 | `Program.cs` implements an explicit graph/AutoMapper adaptation: selected ClientId + SingleOrDefault, scalar DTO pass-through, alerts Select in source order, resolver calls and first SCHOOL selection. The source full methods/mapping are retained as inspection evidence, not claimed to execute intact. Missing requested patient fails safely in this harness; not a newly characterised legacy not-found rule. Excluded GP/HV/practice/centres/telephone fields and their shared graph dependencies remain inventoried in dependencies.md, not displayed or operationally exercised. |
+| CurrentStatusResolver C014; GENDER C079 | Adapter observes nonempty CurrentStatusText resolver argument or empty output; sex emits actual 0/1/2/9 member identities. Missing web enum/status resolver prose is not invented. These are identity/request observations, not exact rendered legacy labels. |
+| Summary/alerts views C013/C019/C020 | Explicit Program.cs observation adapter preserves literal status `7` age suppression (not equated to symbolic stillbirth), age-at-death label, child-alert list calls, named status headings/messages, date-source selection and nested DateFormatStandard-before-message resource calls. `alert-setup` observes ShowAlert AND query != literal `false`; no dialog events, focus, dismissal, native UI or browser execution. Birth-date text uses controlled en-GB `dd-MMM-yyyy`. |
+
+### Infrastructure doubles (actual, not proposed)
+
+- `Compatibility.cs` supplies minimal DTO/entity shapes consumed by extracted expressions; unneeded members of original DTOs are not fabricated. JSON data is deserialised to fresh objects for every request. Raw history rows retain extra saved metadata via JsonExtensionData; no save, update, duplicate/repeat recalculation or measurement-date-overwrite claim is made. Those remain baseline rules.
+- `UnitOfWork.Repository<ChildLocations>` supplies only synthetic authority rows; AsNoTracking is an identity function. Source SingleOrDefault and predicates execute as LINQ-to-Objects. ResultService reconstructs patient, examination description type and given-date navigation from stored flat fixture rows, then executes source filter/order; saved row mapping is identity read-back, not full EF/AutoMapper mapping validation. No SQL translation, DB constraints/transactions/concurrency/collation/order or EF6/Oracle parity claim.
+- `Program.cs` records DefaultAccessForChild as an excluded no-op dependency call. Access-control/session/remote-record decisions, WCF hosting/fault transport, appointment/recall and operational lookup directories are not exercised. Missing graph members cause failures, not assumed operational defaults.
+- `Resource.Format` returns an identity and argument object; CurrentStatusText and EnumResolver are similarly observed requests. Actual legacy resources remain unavailable (SF-G01/G02). Symbolic centre/status constants do not recover numeric identities. These adaptations need reviewer acknowledgement before human approval.
+- `run.py` resolves fresh fixture graphs before invoking C#. It never sends `expected` into the runtime. It sends mixed, unfiltered histories (or reverses the entire input when requested). The explicit KD03-only adapter runs AFTER the original all-KDP query/delegate. This is slice scope, not a rewritten legacy service predicate.
+- Recursive subset comparisons are strict about types, null, strings, booleans and list cardinality. The special ID comparator consumes complete multisets, and date groups consume every observed row without asserting within-tie order. Physical/facet inputs are returned and checked unchanged.
+- **Intentional seed-authored facets**, isolated in Program.cs: Recorded/Not examined from saved reason presence, Initial/Repeat from persisted bool, and Has concern from applicable Heart/Hips/Eyes/Testes/PhysicalGeneral raw value 2 only. No persisted aggregate status is created. These predicates are labelled as enhancements in scenario evidence, not original aggregate clinical logic. No filters, paging, routes or target UI are implemented.
+
+## Limits and unresolved decisions
+
+This is parity evidence for extracted C# rules and disclosed adapters, **not the original Windows/Oracle application**. Fixtures are invented, including deliberately nonvalid SYN-NHS strings and an artificial 23-result history, not typical clinical history. Organisation remains Organisation: health-board concept and wording still require the product owner (SF-G04). Missing legacy resource prose, unsupported numeric constants, UI events, draft Welsh, EF-in-memory target, unverified PostgreSQL/production, local-demo-only and deferred load/performance limitations remain as recorded in `../gaps.md`. Nothing here approves these decisions or launches Convert/Refactor.
+
